      <!-- Detailed Review: Traditional Agency -->
      <div id="traditional-agency" style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">Traditional Agency</h3>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          A traditional agency provides professional services — web design, marketing, branding, advertising — through a team of humans. You pay for expertise, strategy, and execution delivered by designers, developers, copywriters, and account managers. The output is high quality, the process is thorough, and the cost reflects the team size and time involved.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Agencies shine when the project is complex and high-budget. A full brand launch, multi-channel campaign, or enterprise website with custom integrations is exactly what agencies are built for. They bring strategy depth, creative firepower, and project management that a solo operator or AI service can't match.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          The tradeoff is cost and speed. A typical agency website costs $5,000-$15,000 and takes 2-3 months. Ongoing retainers run $2,000-$10,000/month. For a small business or real estate agent, that investment only makes sense if the expected return justifies 5-10x the cost of a BirkyStudio setup. Most agents never need the depth an agency provides — they just need a professional site and a way to answer calls.
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-bottom:16px;">
